0..48 Comment "// Higher-order calls preserve recursive stages."
49..51 Comment "//"
52..117 Comment "// `apply` uses one type parameter for its function and argument."
118..180 Comment "// A call instantiates that parameter at its argument\'s stage."
181..183 Comment "//"
184..221 Comment "// `applyAt` quantifies over a stage."
222..266 Comment "// `predAt` returns at its argument\'s stage."
267..315 Comment "// `sameAt` accepts both arguments at one stage."
316..363 Comment "// A named stage must agree with the arguments."
364..415 Comment "// A higher-order use preserves its supplied stage."
416..418 Comment "//"
